Notebook[
 {Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["HEPCAT SYMBOL", "PacletNameCell"],
       Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["HEPCAT", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/HEPCAT"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
          ButtonBox["Related Guide", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/AmplitudeConstruction"]}],
        "AnchorBar"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.42], Scaled[0.58]}}]],
   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["CompleteFactorization", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Repair physical residue deficits with a bounded simultaneous \
correction fit.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"CompleteFactorization", "[",
         "amplitudes", ",", " ", "channels", ",", " ", "model", "]"}]],
      "InlineFormula"], "  ",
     "Fit corrections against all known physical channels simultaneously."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"CompleteFactorization", "[",
         "preparationReport", ",", " ", "channelsOrReport", ",", " ",
         "model", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Start from prepared inputs \
while retaining discarded expressions and original residue targets."}],
   "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"CompleteFactorization", "[", "input",
         ",", " ", "channels", ",", " ", "model", ",", " ",
         "\"ReturnDetails\"", " ", "->", " ", "True", "]"}]],
      "InlineFormula"], "  ", "Keep the candidate, affine freedom, correction \
directions and validation diagnostics."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The function starts with the \
supplied amplitude, compares every physical residue with its lower-point \
target and solves for correction coefficients together. It does not naively \
add the channel products, which overlap on multiple poles.", "Notes"],
  Cell["When MaxCorrectionTerms is Automatic, an already built and projected \
exchange-symmetry correction union can be admitted within the automatic \
ceiling without rebuilding its sources. CapChanges records the effective \
increase and preserved direction count. This never extends TimeConstraint, \
truncates columns or changes residue and affine-family validation. Explicit \
numerical caps and supplied correction bases retain their limits.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Preparation details provide simplified expressions, original \
expressions and discarded remainders. These are tried before broader \
channel-continuation directions, preserving useful diagram information \
without making a hard-coded process formula.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The correction space is finite and bounded. Alternative reference \
continuations, input reweighting and retained terms can supply additional \
directions. Failure to span a deficit is reported honestly; the function does \
not invent unknown lower amplitudes or arbitrary interactions.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The ordinary successful output is {externalMassRules, expression}. No \
internal shell declaration survives for the complete amplitude. It can be \
passed to PrepareAmplitudes or CompleteHighEnergy.", "Notes"],
  Cell["\"Output\" -> \"Expression\" gives the bare expression. \
\"ReturnDetails\" -> True or \"Output\" -> \"Details\" exposes the fit, \
correction, channel continuations, refinement history and validation. Request \
details when CompleteHighEnergy must retain residue-preserving affine \
freedom.", "Notes"], Cell["\"PolePreference\" biases representation and \
continuation choices. AllPhysical favors physical-only inverse factors; it is \
not permission to return an unchecked expression or a proof that the result \
is globally simplest.", "Notes"], Cell["Identical boson and fermion \
permutations are inferred from ordered external particle identities and the \
model's twice-spin declarations. Equal masses alone cannot identify the \
species. Supply \"ExternalParticles\" when a bare input has lost the ordered \
process metadata.", "Notes"], Cell["Numerical fitting uses locally resolved \
model parameters. A time-based seed is chosen once for Automatic; an integer \
replays the sampling. Independent validation and failed-sample refinement \
guard against a fit that happens to match its training points.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Automatic effort settings bound runtime and correction size. An \
unresolved result normally returns a concise Failure rather than an unchecked \
amplitude. Detailed reports distinguish complete, incomplete and \
underdetermined cases.", "Notes"], Cell["Physical residue agreement leaves \
any genuine pole-free or residue-preserving freedom for CompleteHighEnergy \
and other stated physical constraints. No universal uniqueness claim follows \
from sampled residues alone.", "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CorrectionBasis\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Explicit correction \
expressions whose coefficients may be fitted. Automatic uses bounded \
directions from the supplied diagrams, channels and retained preparation \
data; it does not invent an unrestricted interaction ansatz.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Local numerical parameter \
overrides keyed by model references or string names. Automatic resolves the \
model's variables and dependent functions; fitting and checks do not assign \
global values or replace parameters in the symbolic final amplitude.",
        "TableText"]}, {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Samples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Number of physical cut \
samples or fitting samples, depending on the stage. Automatic completion \
settings choose a bounded process-dependent count; successful fitting is \
followed by separate validation samples.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ValidationSamples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Number of held-out samples \
used after fitting correction coefficients. Automatic chooses a bounded \
workload-dependent allowance; these samples are distinct from the fitting \
equations.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ValidationParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Additional or \
automatically selected local parameter assignments used in independent \
completion validation. They help detect fits tied accidentally to one \
numerical mass or coupling point without changing the symbolic result.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ChannelReferences\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Reference-spinor \
continuations available to factorization completion. Automatic tries a \
bounded set and verifies each on its selected cut; None restricts the fit to \
the literal correction space.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"AlternativeChannels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "}"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Additional compact channel rows to try as \
correction sources if the first completion space does not close. Their \
selected residues must agree with the original targets; they never replace \
those targets.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"BoseSymmetryGroups\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Groups of identical \
external bosons to symmetrize. Automatic infers species and helicity from \
ordered process metadata and the model; {} disables boson exchange projection \
without disabling fermion projection.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FermionSymmetryGroups\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Groups of identical \
external fermions to antisymmetrize with permutation parity signs. Automatic \
uses ordered process metadata and model spin/species declarations; {} \
disables only fermion exchange projection.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ExternalParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Ordered external particle \
names when compact amplitude pairs no longer retain the process. Automatic \
uses recorded metadata or only unambiguous model matches; equal masses alone \
never establish identical species.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"InputReweighting\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether factorization \
completion first fits a scale on the pole-bearing input and a small \
overlap-reduced candidate. Automatic proposes these bounded corrections and \
validates them; None skips them. It is not a rule for averaging diagrams.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RepresentativeSelection\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether completion chooses \
a simpler particular point inside an already validated affine family. \
Automatic performs bounded exact coefficient cancellations while preserving \
its directions and explicit regular input; None retains the original \
particular point.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PolePreference\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Reference and \
representation preference shared by preparation and completion. Automatic \
compares or inherits admissible choices; \"AllPhysical\", \"AllSpurious\" and \
\"Mixed\" bias pole forms, while cyclic/common/independent reference choices \
and None are also available. Required checks remain unchanged.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ChannelCompanions\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether completion first \
tries a small set of source-derived physical-pole correction directions for \
eligible two-leg channels. Automatic gives this attempt a bounded share of \
the existing clock; None skips it. Every original channel must still \
validate.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"PreparationRemainders\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether factorization \
completion first tries grouped discarded preparation terms. Automatic uses \
only retained provenance and a bounded share of the clock; None skips this \
route. The original channel targets remain authoritative.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[
             {"\"ShiftedChannelContinuations\""}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether completion tries \
bounded two-null-leg continuation proposals as correction directions. \
Automatic restricts the attempt to its supported eligibility; False or None \
disables it. Each direction is checked on its own cut and no vanishing \
large-shift boundary is assumed.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxRefinements\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"3"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Maximum rounds that feed failed independent \
validation samples back into the simultaneous factorization equations. Each \
refinement is followed by fresh held-out validation.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RandomSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Random-sampling seed. \
Automatic resolves one time-based seed for the operation; an explicit \
integer, including zero, reproduces the sample choices. Detailed reports \
retain the resolved seed. ComplicateAmplitude uses the legacy symbol key \
RandomSeed; modern construction/checking functions use the string key \
\"RandomSeed\".", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"TimeConstraint\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum elapsed time \
allowed by the operation or stage. Where Automatic is supported it selects a \
finite workload-dependent budget; explicit seconds or supported Infinity \
override it. A timeout is reported, never treated as a successful amplitude."\
, "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxCorrectionTerms\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Bound on the size of the \
fitted correction space. Automatic chooses a finite process-dependent limit; \
explicit values control effort without weakening residue and \
independent-validation requirements.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Parallelization\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Whether independent items \
or checks may use local Wolfram workers. Automatic uses suitable parallel \
work within available resources; False requests serial evaluation, and result \
order is retained.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MaxKernels\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Maximum local Wolfram \
worker kernels available to parallel stages. Automatic respects processor \
availability and license limits; 1 requests serial execution. Worker setup \
and expression transfer can outweigh small jobs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressReporting\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"True"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether preparation and construction stages \
display their progress. False suppresses the live stage display without \
changing the algebra or validation.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProgressFunction\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Optional callback \
receiving stage progress information. Automatic uses the normal progress \
display; callbacks are evaluated on the main kernel rather than independently \
by workers.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ReturnDetails\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to expose optional diagnostic data \
instead of the compact default result. For preparation and factorization \
completion it retains provenance, directions and validation and takes \
precedence over Output; for export it returns file paths and build/run \
results.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Output\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Amplitude\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Choose the amount and \
shape of returned information. Defaults are a compact check table, prepared \
input forms, a completed {externalMassRules, expression} pair, or a bare \
constructed expression; \"Details\" preserves diagnostics and provenance.",
        "TableText"]}}, GridBoxAlignment ->
      {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}}, GridBoxItemSize ->
      {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19], Scaled[0.58]}},
     GridBoxDividers -> {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]],
   "3ColumnTableMod"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["Basic Examples", "ExampleSection"],
  Cell["The explicit staged QED workflow retains preparation information.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"qedModel", " ", "=", " ",
      "ReadModel", "[", "modelDirectory", ",", " ", "2", "]", ";", "\n",
      "process", " ", "=", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ",
      "\"A.+\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", "}", ";", "\n", "diagrams", " ", "=",
      " ", "CreateDiagrams", "[", "process", ",", " ", "qedModel", "]", ";",
      "\n", "amplitudes", " ", "=", " ", "diagramAmplitudes", "[",
      "diagrams", "]", ";", "\n", "channels", " ", "=", " ",
      "FactorizationAmplitudeChannels", "[", "process", ",", " ", "qedModel",
      "]", ";", "\n", "prepared", " ", "=", " ", "PrepareAmplitudes", "[",
      "amplitudes", ",", " ", "qedModel", ",", " ", "\"ReturnDetails\"", " ",
      "->", " ", "True", "]", ";", "\n", "factorized", " ", "=", " ",
      "CompleteFactorization", "[", "prepared", ",", " ", "channels", ",",
      " ", "qedModel", ",", " ", "\"ReturnDetails\"", " ", "->", " ", "True",
      "]", ";", "\n", "factorized"}]], "Input"],
  Cell["This example writes files, starts a longer calculation, or requires \
an optional external tool. Evaluate it when you want to perform that \
operation.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell["A declared scalar contact amplitude requires no pole correction.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"scalarModel", " ", "=", " ", "{",
      "{", "{", "\"scalar\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ",
      "1", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "1", ",",
      " ", "\"\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", "}", "}", ",", " ",
      "{", "{", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ", "\"s\"", ",", " ",
      "\"s\"", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "7", "}", "}", ",", " ", "{", "}",
      ",", " ", "{", "}", "}", ";", "\n", "externalRules", " ", "=", " ",
      "Thread", "[", "(", "Mass", " ", "/@", " ", "Range", "[", "4", "]",
      ")", " ", "->", " ", "0", "]", ";", "\n", "CompleteFactorization", "[",
